<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Backup and transfer policy for Android 12 (API 31) and above.

    AURIX keeps every non-secret preference in one SharedPreferences file,
    `FlutterSharedPreferences.xml` — the fixed name the shared_preferences
    plugin uses on Android for `SharedPreferences.getInstance()`. That file is
    excluded here so a reinstall genuinely starts from nothing.

    The reason is the Dynamic Island. It is an opt-in feature that must be OFF
    on a fresh install and must never switch itself on, and `aurix.settings
    .dynamic_island` lives in this file. With `android:allowBackup` left at its
    default of true and no rules in place, Android's cloud restore hands the old
    value straight back: uninstall with the island ON, reinstall, and the app
    would come up with the island already on — from restored data, without the
    user ever touching the switch. That is precisely the automatic enable the
    feature is not allowed to do.

    This costs more than the one flag, and deliberately so: backup rules operate
    on whole files, and Android offers no way to exclude a single key. Theme,
    streaming quality, crossfade and the rest reset on reinstall alongside it.
    Splitting the island's flag into its own excluded prefs file would need a
    platform channel of AURIX's own, since the plugin's file name is fixed —
    a lot of native surface to keep one boolean out of a backup, and one more
    thing to get wrong, when "a reinstalled app starts at its defaults" is
    honest behaviour on its own.

    Tokens are unaffected either way. They live in flutter_secure_storage, not
    here.

    `aurix_native.xml` is excluded for a related reason. It holds one flag —
    whether AURIX has already asked for POST_NOTIFICATIONS — which exists to
    tell "not asked yet" apart from "asked and refused for good". Restoring it
    onto a fresh install would carry over a refusal the new install's system
    permission state knows nothing about, and the app would report the
    notification as permanently denied while Android was still perfectly willing
    to show the dialog.

    Both sections are excluded on purpose. `cloud-backup` is the reinstall path
    the rule exists for; `device-transfer` is a new handset, where an island
    arriving already switched on would be the same surprise wearing a different
    hat.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="FlutterSharedPreferences.xml"/>
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="aurix_native.xml"/>
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="FlutterSharedPreferences.xml"/>
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="aurix_native.xml"/>
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
